  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Let $S=\\{-7,0,3,8\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nf(3)=-11,\\,f(-7)=-5,\\,f(8)=2,\\,f(0)=12.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)=$\n{{field-4}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nHere, the outputs are $-11,$ $-5,$ $2,$ and $12.$ \n\n- The largest output is $12,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$\n\n- The smallest output is $-11,$ and it occurs at $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =12 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =-11 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
